@startuml
title Flyweight / Cache of shared objects

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Share fine-grained objects efficiently;
separate intrinsic (shared) from extrinsic (context) state.

**Motivation**:
Large numbers of similar objects (e.g., characters, tiles).

**Applicability**:
High-volume, immutable intrinsic state shared; extrinsic state passed per use.

**Participants**:
FlyweightFactory manages shared instances in a pool.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Drastic memory reduction.
Cons: Complex separation of state; requires disciplined usage.

**Implementation Notes**:
Ensure immutability of intrinsic state.
Use key-based caches; careful synchronization.

**Known Uses**:
Java Integer.valueOf, String interning.
Graphics engines (sprites, glyphs).

**Related Patterns**:
Prototype (copy), Object Pool, Immutable.

endlegend

interface Flyweight {
  +operation(extrinsicState)
}

class ConcreteFlyweight
Flyweight <|.. ConcreteFlyweight

class FlyweightFactory {
  -pool : Map<Key, Flyweight>
  +get(key) : Flyweight
}

FlyweightFactory o-- Flyweight : shares
@enduml